      "episode_id": "VR-478143",
      "has_more": false,
      "messages": [
        {
          "content": "Juror-1 independent check of the Unit 4 electricity readings, from the case record alone (round 1):\n\nSeptember consumption per meter, from the 1 Sep and 30 Sep actual readings:\n  M-0412 main hall: 50,977.0 - 48,213.6 = 2,763.4 kWh\n  M-0413 annex: 12,902.9 - 12,040.2 = 862.7 kWh\n  Total across both meters: 3,626.1 kWh\n\n3,626.1 kWh is more than 3,500 kWh, so the claim as worded holds. The margin is 126.1 kWh, about 3.6% of the threshold - narrow, but the arithmetic is exact to one decimal place and the record states these are actual readings.\n\nOn the 15 Sep estimated reading for M-0412: it does not affect the result. Consumption is the difference between the 1 Sep and 30 Sep readings, both of which the record says are actual readings taken by the site engineer, so the estimated midpoint cancels: (49,502.0 - 48,213.6) + (50,977.0 - 49,502.0) = 2,763.4 kWh, identical to the direct difference. The note that consumption is billed from actual readings only is consistent with that.\n\nSensitivity I checked: neither meter alone exceeds the threshold (2,763.4 and 862.7 kWh), so the claim depends on correctly aggregating both meters, which the record supports - Unit 4 has no other meters and neither rolled over or was replaced. If the 15 Sep estimate were wrongly treated as the period-end reading, the total would be only 1,719.7 kWh, but that is not the period end.\n\nOn this record the claim is supported. I find no unsupported element and no basis to dispute it.",
          "content_hash": "0xe026ad404c8bbbdd83b52a36e922e7bc344ed4922a752f168502aefb36db41d1",
          "created_at_ms": 1793326248584,
          "message_id": "7a6fe500-d937-4d16-a33b-bdfdc550b7dc",
          "round_num": 1,
          "sender_id": "juror-1",
          "sequence": 1
        },
        {
          "content": "Challenger's review of the Unit 4 electricity claim against the Northfield Business Park readings for 1-30 September 2026:\n\nPeriod consumption is measured from actual readings only. Both the 1 September and 30 September readings are stated to be actual readings taken by the site engineer on both meters, so the mid-period estimate does not affect the month total:\n\n  M-0412 (main hall): 50,977.0 - 48,213.6 = 2,763.4 kWh\n  M-0413 (annex):     12,902.9 - 12,040.2 =   862.7 kWh\n  Total across both meters: 3,626.1 kWh\n\n3,626.1 exceeds 3,500 by 126.1 kWh, so the claim that Unit 4 consumed more than 3,500 kWh in September across its two meters is supported. The site note confirms Unit 4 has no other meters and neither meter rolled over or was replaced, so no adjustment is needed.\n\nOne caution for anyone checking this: the 15 September main-hall figure (49,502.0) is flagged as estimated because the meter cupboard was locked. It should not be used as an endpoint. Measuring only 15-30 September would give 1,475.0 + 431.4 = 1,906.4 kWh, which is not the month's consumption; and consumption is billed from actual readings only. The correct month total uses the actual 1 and 30 September readings, giving 3,626.1 kWh.\n\nOn this evidence I am not challenging the claim.",
          "content_hash": "0x6a936ee02745b21595d8753f9da0b1af798d6b8f2150c044d247162c79075bf7",
          "created_at_ms": 1793326260532,
          "message_id": "5cf870e4-7386-4f6c-acef-29defa9b4236",
          "round_num": 1,
          "sender_id": "challenger",
          "sequence": 2
        },
        {
          "content": "Juror-3 independent check of the Unit 4 electricity readings, Northfield Business Park, September 2026, from the case record alone (round 1).\n\nClaim tested: \"Unit 4 consumed more than 3,500 kWh in September across its two meters.\"\n\nConsumption must be measured actual-to-actual (1 Sep to 30 Sep), since the record states consumption is billed from actual readings only:\n- M-0412 (main hall): 50,977.0 - 48,213.6 = 2,763.4 kWh\n- M-0413 (annex): 12,902.9 - 12,040.2 = 862.7 kWh\n- Total across both meters = 3,626.1 kWh\n\n3,626.1 exceeds 3,500, so the claim holds, by a margin of 126.1 kWh.\n\nThe 15 September main-hall figure is marked estimated because the cupboard was locked. It is an intermediate point, so it cancels out of a 1 Sep to 30 Sep difference: 1,288.4 + 1,475.0 = 2,763.4, giving the identical total of 3,626.1. So the estimate does not affect the result either way.\n\nTwo readings I rejected: using M-0412 alone (2,763.4) would fall below 3,500, but the claim explicitly covers both meters; and summing the closing readings (50,977.0 + 12,902.9) is meaningless because those are cumulative register values, not consumption. The record confirms no other meters, no rollover and no replacement, so no adjustment is needed.",
          "content_hash": "0xc96b7fbeb95574ca134859f8e08ce9a979b2fd134bdfc433306f254c9d73d4b8",
          "created_at_ms": 1793326272204,
          "message_id": "357724bb-be97-49c5-947a-0093e757fa9d",
          "round_num": 1,
          "sender_id": "juror-3",
          "sequence": 3
        },
        {
          "content": "Juror-2 independent check of the Unit 4 electricity readings, Northfield Business Park, 1-30 September 2026, from the case record alone (round 1):\n\nConsumption is the difference between the 1 Sep and 30 Sep readings, both stated to be actual readings taken by the site engineer on both meters:\n  M-0412 main hall: 50,977.0 - 48,213.6 = 2,763.4 kWh\n  M-0413 annex: 12,902.9 - 12,040.2 = 862.7 kWh\n  Total across both meters: 2,763.4 + 862.7 = 3,626.1 kWh\n\n3,626.1 kWh exceeds 3,500 kWh by 126.1 kWh, so the claim as worded holds. The margin is narrow - about 3.6% of the threshold - but the readings are exact to one decimal place and both endpoints are actual readings.\n\nOn the 15 Sep estimated M-0412 figure: it cancels out and cannot change the result. Splitting the period at the estimate gives (49,502.0 - 48,213.6) + (50,977.0 - 49,502.0) = 1,288.4 + 1,475.0 = 2,763.4 kWh, identical to the direct difference. The estimate is not an endpoint and the record says consumption is billed from actual readings only.\n\nSensitivity: neither meter alone clears the threshold (2,763.4 and 862.7 kWh), so the claim depends on aggregating both meters, which the record supports - Unit 4 has no other meters and neither rolled over or was replaced in the period. Using the estimate as a period end would wrongly give 1,719.7 kWh, but that is not the month total.\n\nOn this record the claim is supported. I find no unsupported element and no basis to dispute it.",
          "content_hash": "0x6fa5bc296cd6b6286b04d92dfbbed07ee96486590181a15b6ea7b30833494c72",
          "created_at_ms": 1793326300105,
          "message_id": "826c4375-1787-48d9-ab0c-94cc30e95c02",
          "round_num": 1,
          "sender_id": "juror-2",
          "sequence": 4
        }
      ],
